
1. Scope & priority

	•	Do you want health checks on all systems in the diagram, or start with a subset (e.g. just TI+ core + security gateway)?
	•	Which systems are causing the most pain today — where do devs spend the most manual-check time?
	•	Is this meant to replace manual checks entirely, or supplement them (early warning only)?

2. Ownership & access

	•	Who owns each system for approvals — can QA get credentials/API access to DBs, JMS queues, SFTP servers, or does that need to go through Infra/DBA/Security?
	•	For downstream systems we don't own (SWIFT, AML, PRISM, SAP GL) — do we have any access at all, or are we limited to indirect checks (e.g. file/log-based)?
	•	Who should receive alerts, and who is expected to act on them (QA just detects, or also triages)?

3. Tooling & infrastructure

	•	Does the bank already have a monitoring tool (Nagios, Zabbix, Dynatrace, AppDynamics, etc.) we should build into, instead of creating something new?
	•	Where should scripts run from — a dedicated server/VM, existing CI/CD (Jenkins), or QA's local environment?
	•	Is there a preferred language/stack (Node.js vs Python vs existing team tooling)?
	•	What's the alerting channel — email, Slack/Teams, ticketing tool (ServiceNow/Jira)?

4. Environments

	•	Is this for Production only, or also UAT/SIT/DR environments?
	•	Are there different endpoints/credentials per environment we need to account for?

5. Thresholds & expectations

	•	What response time / downtime is considered acceptable before it's flagged an issue?
	•	Are there existing SLAs (per system) we should align alert thresholds to, or do we define them ourselves?
	•	How false-positive-tolerant should this be — is a few false alerts a week OK while we tune it, or does it need to be near-perfect from day one?

6. Security & compliance

	•	Any restrictions on storing credentials for automated scripts (e.g. must use a vault/secrets manager)?
	•	Any change-management or approval process required before scripts can run against Production systems?

7. Success criteria & timeline

	•	How will success be measured — reduced manual-check time, faster detection, fewer incidents escalated?
	•	Is there a deadline or is this open-ended / phased?
	•	Do you want a proof-of-concept on a few systems first before scaling to the full list?

Suggested opening line to lead with: "Before I build out the automation plan, I want to align on scope, access, and tooling so we don't rework it later — can we go through a few quick questions?"

